ull},{"content_hash":"c4c8e0b0efc4ba206bb2c9009f4e7b5bf3ac3820366cb9fa90c169713e5998eb","event_uuid":"788a5255-f0f6-41ab-8373-d9f420022b6b","position":{"commit_sha":"f36f1559aead0749ee23681451641af381357b7d","position":"1787335405174076001-788a5255-f0f6-41ab-8373-d9f420022b6b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"bfb54bcd823e99579ab4e041bef2662d108cbddbda9a37ac2310045dfe246f7c","event_uuid":"028daec8-95cd-463f-8ede-2e1465ec902c","position":{"commit_sha":"895cdfd3549ace4a9bcfea898b042b6f45ce01f2","position":"1787335412353507001-028daec8-95cd-463f-8ede-2e1465ec902c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"77edb38dea459029f27c32378f0981cf8a6397e569041e4bd8e1472de5eeee0a","event_uuid":"e89f54d0-780d-4019-8742-5972f6b0e4be","position":{"commit_sha":"7bbf00eea60adf97123fd942f87e9ba2be95939f","position":"1787336172491377001-e89f54d0-780d-4019-8742-5972f6b0e4be"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"6cb97e8c6aa02e4446b26290a53b584052da6b0252eb4749fcdb7e722153c9ba","event_uuid":"774ee627-aea1-4281-b268-bda04ea24b9c","position":{"commit_sha":"64f9efc26fb57902dcc6edbe59868c34150644e9","position":"1787336975691264241-774ee627-aea1-4281-b268-bda04ea24b9c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a80a412979bf864cddd1afc9da86b8cb9f1f8275c20ea9185ea508f03d7ff806","event_uuid":"61c79fe1-9d1e-40c2-ba90-f67f60ea4e57","position":{"commit_sha":"d0522a1ef29807d2bc55f0c1105159c90177ebc7","position":"1787338225434611001-61c79fe1-9d1e-40c2-ba90-f67f60ea4e57"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"eb2ddcec099ae813de3a5dd9951cdb346dc6ff141dc6c7188ca32ecbd1567bd2","event_uuid":"5b315605-aec4-4173-80fa-be5987b73e0c","position":{"commit_sha":"7cf30bedc358e7ed6823ccd4d54736a2290de502","position":"1787338868966888001-5b315605-aec4-4173-80fa-be5987b73e0c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e47be115db9ee5781c0d7a9eaa43c9dbc47d796ce0a4dea118cafb38fe5c3a33","event_uuid":"abde262e-3b7b-4d16-b588-27250fb330ec","position":{"commit_sha":"084c29d5fb0fd1393fc56f743f44ceda5c64af16","position":"1787338872520560001-abde262e-3b7b-4d16-b588-27250fb330ec"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (worktree fix-17c3, HEAD 1ab859777a) — CONFIRMED at runtime.\n\nMechanism (one root cause, two visible facets): the outbound comment differ produces its two\nbody-equality keys with DIFFERENT decode compositions.\n\n- Jira side (outbound_comments.py:527): `_normalize_comment_body(fetched_wire)` ->\n  `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` -> `adf_to_text` — never escapes.\n- Local side (outbound_comments.py:571-573): `_normalize_comment_body(\n  codec.normalize_outbound(sanitizer.fit_comment(body)))`. Under\n  `rich_text_cutover=\"cloud\"`, `AdfCodec(rich=True).normalize_outbound` is\n  `adf_to_markdown(markdown_to_adf(text))` — a markdown round trip that ESCAPES\n  markdown-active characters and rewrites autolinks (`[link](http://x)` ->\n  `[link](<http://x>)`).\n\nDiscriminating runtime experiment: captured the REAL wire from `acli_cli_ops.add_comment`\n(only `acli_subprocess._run_acli` stubbed) with the in-limit markdown body from this ticket.\nResult: local key carries the escapes, landed key does not, `_diff_comments` re-emits the\nalready-landed body (1 duplicate mutation). Exactly reproduces the recorded repro.\n\nDeeper send-path fact the experiment surfaced (same root cause, explains why the rich round\ntrip can NEVER match): the send path encodes the DECORATED body\n(`to_wire(fit_preserving_marker(decorate(body), fit_outbound))`, acli_cli_ops.py:531), and the\ndecoration `<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->` is an HTML comment, so `markdown_to_adf`'s\ndocumented content-preservation fallback (adf.py:421-446) degrades the WHOLE document to the\nplain `text_to_adf` encode — the landed wire is the literal markdown source in plain\nparagraphs, while the local key is the rich round trip of the UNDECORATED body.\n\nFix (matches the recorded direction \"produce both keys with one decoder\"): derive the local\nkey by predicting the wire as-sent and decoding it with the SAME decoder as the Jira side:\n`_normalize_comment_body(codec.to_wire(_decorate_outbound_comment(sanitizer.fit_comment(body))))`.\n`decorate(fit_comment(body)) == fit_preserving_marker(decorate(body), fit)` in every\nnon-pathological case because `fit_comment` (= `fit_comment_as_sent`) is that composition with\nthe decoration taken back off. Verified in an 8-cell matrix (cutover off/cloud x in-limit md /\nover-length md / plain in-limit / oversize plain): new key == landed key in ALL cells; old key\ndiverged in 3 cloud cells; every cell where the old key matched still matches (no loosening,\nno shifted in-limit plain key). Send-path behavior untouched.\n\nPlan-review advisory (G6) noted: the pathological `fit_comment_as_sent` branch (bare\ndecoration itself does not fit) would make re-decoration diverge from the wire — unreachable\nfor real comments (the ~30-char decoration against a 32,000-char serialized budget); dedup in\nthat cell is best-effort either way.\n\nDefect attribution (caused_by): commit 27b868ba55 \"Append-only comment sync with comment-ID\nmap\", ticket 789c-1251-fc21-4cf6 (emersed-specific-mutt). That change simultaneously (a) moved\nthe send path onto codec ADF encoding of the decorated body and (b) flipped `_resolve_codec`'s\ndefault so the LOCAL key routes through the flag-governed `normalize_outbound` — while leaving\nthe Jira-side decode on `normalize_rich_text`/`adf_to_text`. The asymmetry is born there:\nbefore it, the local key never passed through a markdown round trip. `git log -S` over both\nkey sites names it directly; a32a (3f5880cea9) only introduced the identity-default codec seam\nand created no divergence. Not attributable to e339-9709 (which fixed the FIT divergence and\nfiled this ticket as its residual).","timestamp":1787335405174076001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix implemented and validated (pre-push). Change: (1) _diff_comments compare_body now derives the LOCAL dedup key as _normalize_comment_body(codec.to_wire(_decorate_outbound_comment(sanitizer.fit_comment(body)))) — the one-decoder form: predict the exact as-sent wire (decorate → fit → encode, matching acli_cli_ops.add_comment) and decode it through the SAME _normalize_comment_body the Jira-side key uses. (2) _IdentityCodec gained a to_wire identity so the identity default keeps its no-op semantics. (3) Docstrings (module, _resolve_codec, _diff_comments) updated to describe the to_wire-based derivation. Send path untouched. RED→GREEN: 3 new tests in test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py (in-limit markdown dedup under cloud cutover; genuinely-new markdown still emitted, parametrized off/cloud; over-length markdown truncation-notice facet) — capture-from-real-send-path pattern, only _run_acli stubbed. Both new dedup tests failed pre-fix (duplicate mutation emitted), all 12 pass post-fix; mutation check (old expression seeded back) turns them RED again. Validation: 479 tests across diffing/, length-convergence (cloud+DC), rich_text_codec, backend_neutrality, acli_comment_adf_encode, comment enrichment/inbound-diff, dc_comment_ceiling all pass; make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (619 files); complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0 (1 allowed stale); module 605 LOC < 800 cap. Live repro re-run post-fix: mutations emitted over already-landed markdown body = 0 (was 1). Next: commit + Gerrit push.","timestamp":1787336172491377001}],"created_at":1787305651742009001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6daf551e-a7c6-4461-b2d6-a81246090a38","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e339-9709-15fe-419a"},{"link_uuid":"028daec8-95cd-463f-8ede-2e1465ec902c","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"789c-1251-fc21-4cf6"},{"link_uuid":"774ee627-aea1-4281-b268-bda04ea24b9c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b6df-7e3b-34b0-4abd"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered while proving `abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey` (e339-9709-15fe-419a). Independent of\nthat ticket's FIT divergence: under `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"` (this project's\nsetting, `rebar.toml:87`) the outbound comment differ decodes the two sides of its\nbody-equality key with DIFFERENT decoders, so a markdown comment WELL WITHIN the length limit\nnever matches its own landed body.\n\n- **Local side** — `_diff_comments` computes `codec.normalize_outbound(...)`. In rich mode\n  `AdfCodec.normalize_outbound` is a markdown round trip, which ESCAPES markdown-active\n  characters and rewrites autolinks.\n- **Jira side** — `_normalize_comment_body` calls `inbound_mapper.normalize_rich_text`\n  (`inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` -> `adf_to_text`), which does NOT escape.\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\nDriving the real `AdfCodec(rich=True)` and `_JiraInbound` on current main\n(worktree `fix-sakimonkey-dedupkey`), with an in-limit markdown body:\n\n```\nlocal key : '# Head\\n\\nSome *bold* text and a [link](<http://x>) plus `code`.\\n\\n- a\\n- b'\nlanded key: '# Head\\n\\nSome *bold* text and a [link](http://x) plus `code`.\\n\\n- a\\n- b'\nEQUAL?    : False\n```\n\nThe same asymmetry escapes the truncation notice: the local key carries\n`\\[truncated by reconciler\\]` where the landed body carries `[truncated by reconciler]`.\n\n## Confirmed root cause (Phase 1, worktree fix-17c3)\n\nReproduced deterministically by capturing the real send path (`acli_cli_ops.add_comment`,\nonly `_run_acli` stubbed): the landed wire is `to_wire(fit_preserving_marker(DECORATED\nbody))`, and because the decoration `<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->` is an HTML comment,\n`markdown_to_adf`'s documented content-preservation fallback (`adf.py`, `markdown_to_adf`)\ndegrades the WHOLE document to the plain `text_to_adf` encode. The Jira-side key decodes that\nwire with `adf_to_text` (no escaping). The local key instead round-trips the UNDECORATED body\nthrough `adf_to_markdown(markdown_to_adf(...))` (`outbound_comments.py`, `_diff_comments`\n`compare_body`), which both escapes markdown-active characters AND renders rich — two\ndivergences from the landed form with one root cause: the two keys are produced by different\ndecode compositions.\n\n## Fix plan (one decoder)\n\nIn `_diff_comments`, derive the LOCAL key by predicting the exact wire the send path produces\nand decoding it with the SAME decoder already used on the fetched Jira side:\n`_normalize_comment_body(codec.to_wire(_decorate_outbound_comment(sanitizer.fit_comment(body))))`\nreplacing `_normalize_comment_body(codec.normalize_outbound(sanitizer.fit_comment(body)))`.\n`to_wire` is already part of the `RichTextCodec` Protocol; `_IdentityCodec` grows an identity\n`to_wire` so the no-codec fallback is unchanged. Send-path behavior is NOT touched — this is\nkey derivation only. Verified at runtime across the 8-cell matrix (cutover off/cloud x\n{in-limit md, over-length md, plain in-limit, oversize plain}): the new key equals the landed\nkey in every cell; the old key diverges in 3 cloud cells; every cell where the old key already\nmatched still matches (no loosening, no shifted in-limit plain key).\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED test first: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py`\n  gains cases under `REBAR_RECONCILER_RICH_TEXT_CUTOVER=cloud` with an in-limit markdown body:\n  the landed side CAPTURED from the real `add_comment` (only `_run_acli` stubbed, same pattern\n  as the existing tests in that file), asserting `_diff_comments` emits no duplicate mutation\n  (RED pre-fix) and that a genuinely new markdown comment is still emitted (counter-regression).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/ tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_dc_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (no new/increased entries)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The differ's two comparison keys are produced by the same decode under every\n      `rich_text_cutover` setting — verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py -q`.\n- [x] A test drives an in-limit markdown comment through the differ with the cutover ON and\n      asserts no duplicate mutation is emitted (RED on current code) — checked: run the new\n      test at the pre-fix commit and observe the failure, then GREEN post-fix.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py","reason":"one-decoder local dedup key derivation (to_wire + shared _normalize_comment_body); _IdentityCodec gains identity to_wire"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py","reason":"RED-first in-limit markdown dedup cases under cloud cutover, landed side captured from the real send path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b6df-7e3b-34b0-4abd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5b315605-aec4-4173-80fa-be5987b73e0c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"17c3-2f6e-a5e0-438c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud comment dedup key is markdown-escaped on one side only","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9dd2acc8-3315-4b53-b289-c3fe8b0cd9d0","a9d2f3c5-a8bb-4af9-94ce-66e2a4c03b81","137e09ca-90af-4e54-834a-6684ecf6fb33","0b7a5c56-d5a1-4a8b-813d-3cce4e0e7a1f","b9273471-17de-484d-9b54-ba313ec44fad","58a91287-f1d2-43a3-8d3f-c0bac4dd61db","788a5255-f0f6-41ab-8373-d9f420022b6b","028daec8-95cd-463f-8ede-2e1465ec902c","e89f54d0-780d-4019-8742-5972f6b0e4be","774ee627-aea1-4281-b268-bda04ea24b9c","61c79fe1-9d1e-40c2-ba90-f67f60ea4e57","5b315605-aec4-4173-80fa-be5987b73e0c","abde262e-3b7b-4d16-b588-27250fb330ec"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787341652460475001,"uuid":"86f06634-9532-447f-9638-d19fb752a2f3"}